# The runtime ends the VR session on its own (#146): SteamVR quitting the app (stopping, then exiting after
# xrEndSession), then the runtime itself shutting down (instance loss pending). The game goes on in flat mode and
# names each cause in arx.log; the run then quits through the channel ("Quit requested: the test channel's quit
# command") and must end cleanly - the exit hook reports nothing.
# The window never minimises on a focus loss in VR (#406) and follows cfg.ini's minimize_on_focus_lost again once the
# game is flat (#606; status window.minimizeOnFocusLost and settings.minimizeOnFocusLost: window-minimize-restore.xrs).
@sim idle
@args --loadlevel 10

@until state eq GAMEPLAY 60s
@until vr.sessionState eq focused 30s
@remember cfg settings.minimizeOnFocusLost
@assert window.minimizeOnFocusLost eq false

vr-sim session exiting
@log OpenXR session ended by the runtime \(exiting\), continuing in flat mode 10s
@until vr.sessionState eq none 10s
@frames 10
@assert state eq GAMEPLAY
@assert window.minimizeOnFocusLost eq {cfg}

# Without a session the runtime can still go away: the instance follows
vr-sim runtime lost
@log OpenXR runtime is shutting down \(instance loss pending\), continuing in flat mode 10s
@frames 10
@assert state eq GAMEPLAY
@assert window.minimizeOnFocusLost eq {cfg}
@nolog ExitTrace
